WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.231 --> 00:00:06.703
NARRATOR: In 1995, Tony Hawk
wins gold in the first X Games

00:00:06.736 --> 00:00:09.439
and goes on to
dominate the decade.

00:00:10.073 --> 00:00:12.375
In 1999 he cranks it up a notch,

00:00:12.408 --> 00:00:16.579
attempting a never
before done trick, the 900.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:20.483
HAWK: A 900 is
a two and a half spin rotation

00:00:20.516 --> 00:00:23.987
sort of summersault in the air,
holding onto your skateboard.

00:00:25.855 --> 00:00:27.390
The thing that makes it
the most challenging is that

00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:30.827
you are blind to
your landing zone twice.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.297
DUNCAN (over speaker):
Yeah, 900!

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.699
HAWK: I had no plans
of doing 900 at X Games.

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:38.768
I think it was
the onsite announcer,

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.137
Dave Duncan that said,
"Oh let's see that 900,"

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.472
'cause he knew
I'd been trying it.

00:00:42.505 --> 00:00:44.907
DUNCAN (over speaker): Run back,
Tony's got a shot at it.

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:46.275
Can he do it?

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:47.577
HAWK: And so I just
started trying it more

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.647
to appease the crowd and to
appease Dave on the mic, like,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.948
here's what it looks like.

00:00:51.981 --> 00:00:55.918
DUNCAN (over speaker):
900! 900, this could be it.

00:00:55.952 --> 00:00:59.322
Oh. The closest one.

00:00:59.355 --> 00:01:00.890
(cheering)

00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:02.125
We're not worthy.

00:01:02.158 --> 00:01:03.893
SEMIAO: When he'd go up and
start flipping it was like...

00:01:03.926 --> 00:01:05.595
(gasps).

00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:08.364
(sighs).

00:01:09.365 --> 00:01:10.833
HAWK: Something
inside me just said,

00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:13.469
"You're either making this or
they're gonna cart you off of

00:01:13.503 --> 00:01:16.472
the ramp to the hospital,"

00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:20.343
those were the only two
endings to that night for me.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.579
DUNCAN (over speaker):
Tony, Tony, Tony, Tony, Tony,

00:01:23.613 --> 00:01:25.815
history in the making.

00:01:25.848 --> 00:01:28.518
SEMIAO: The 900 was
revolutionary 'cause

00:01:28.551 --> 00:01:31.421
it had never been done before.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.725
My heart was in mouth.

00:01:35.758 --> 00:01:38.194
I didn't want him to be
taken away in an ambulance,

00:01:38.227 --> 00:01:40.697
I wanted him to land it.

00:01:42.131 --> 00:01:43.366
HAWK: At one point I
thought it wasn't possible

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:46.202
and it was just like,
I wasn't gonna give up.

00:01:51.741 --> 00:01:54.811
(cheering)

00:01:57.046 --> 00:02:00.650
SEMIAO: And when he
did it, that pure shock.

00:02:04.387 --> 00:02:07.323
HAWK: When I made it, I saw all
my peers rushing towards me and

00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:10.159
it was like that,
that made it real.

00:02:11.561 --> 00:02:14.931
SEMIAO: And that's how
you achieve legendary status.

00:02:14.964 --> 00:02:17.433
It was big for the X Games,
it was big for Tony Hawk,

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.069
it was big for skateboarding,
like today we'd say,

00:02:20.103 --> 00:02:22.171
"It went viral," you know, and,

00:02:22.205 --> 00:02:25.842
and that was, was
really a seminal moment.

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:27.643
(cheering)

00:02:27.677 --> 00:02:28.711
DUNCAN (over speaker):
What you got to say?

00:02:28.745 --> 00:02:30.046
How do you feel right now?

00:02:30.079 --> 00:02:31.347
HAWK (over speaker): If
it weren't for you people,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.117
I would have never
made that, I swear to God.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.185
(cheering)

